       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. OTC labeling caps it at 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n\n- **400 mg four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day total.\n- **800 mg three times daily:** 2,400 mg/day, a common prescription regimen.\n- **800 mg four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1600 mg/day divided differently:** for example, 800 mg twice daily.\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
