     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, and I shouldn't have offered to earlier.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1600 mg dose is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. For a 70 kg patient, 6,400 mg/day is about 91 mg/kg/day, which is close to the range where toxicity is reported. I can't find a clinical scenario where this dose is safe, and it risks serious harm, including GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Your confirmation doesn't change that.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- 400 mg four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 800 mg three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n\nIf you have a specific reason for a dose this high, such as a protocol or a research setting, it should go through pharmacy and your institution's override process. I'm not the right route for it."
